    questions: [
      PracticeQuestion(
        scenario: "Question 1: (a) Explain four reasons why students abuse drugs.\n"
            "(b) State three effects of substance abuse.\n"
            "(BECE 2005 Q4)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ Refusal to stick to medical advice: Some students refuse to seek the advice of a qualified medical practitioner in order that they may do self-medication.\n"
            "⦿ Emotional stress situation: Students abuse drugs so that they can control their emotions such as shyness, anger, etc.\n"
            "⦿ Ignorance: Students abuse drugs out of ignorance or not knowing the negative effects of drug abuse.\n"
            "⦿ Peer influence: Students abuse drugs due to peer pressure or seeing their friends in engaging in such activities.\n"
            "⦿ Economic stress situation: Situations such as unemployment and poverty may encourage students to abuse drugs so that they can forget their present problems.\n"
            "⦿ Broken homes: The absence of parents in the home to guide and counsel students can lead to students abusing drugs.\n"
            "⦿ For high academic achievement: Students sometimes think that certain drugs can help them to stay awake and study late into the night so that they can perform well in the exams.\n"
            "⦿ Lack of recreational activities and facilities can also lead to drug abuse.\n"
            "⦿ Lack of self-control or self-discipline: Some students abuse drugs simply because they are not able to control their desires.\n"
            "⦿ Rebellion against authority: Students resort to illegal drugs to enable them become bold and fearless so that they may rebel against authorities.\n"
            "⦿ Advertisements: Advertisements on radio, television and other media encourage students to buy and use the drugs without medical approval.\n"
            "⦿ Curiosity: The tendency to abuse drugs may also be due to the desire to experience its side effects.\n"
            "⦿ Enhancing their self-esteem or image.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ Loss of life or severe clinical health problems: The abuse of substances such as marijuana and other illegal drugs can cause the user to lose his or her life (death). That is, it can make the user suffer from stroke, heart beat or cancer, lung cancer, etc. leading to his or her death.\n"
            "⦿ Reduced workplace productivity and high absenteeism: The psychological problems associated with abuse of substances such as marijuana, cocaine, etc. reduce the ability of the users to perform efficiently at workplaces. This leads to absenteeism or low output in the country.\n"
            "⦿ Propensity to engage in social vices: The abuse of substances can have negative impact on the users to engage in social vices such as theft, rebellion against authority, rape, etc.\n"
            "⦿ Organ damage and mental challenges: It may also lead to health problems. That is, people who use substances such as tramadol, marijuana, cocaine, etc. can suffer from heart problems, cancer and mental challenges.\n"
            "⦿ Brain damage and physical deformaties: The use of illegal drugs such as cocaine, marijuana, tramadol, etc. can deform a person or cause physical damage to the body of a person. For instance, it can damage the brain of a person leading to lapses in his or her memory or madness.\n"
            "⦿ Dependency and addiction: Abuse of substances such as marijuana, tramadol, alcohol, etc. may cause the user to become dependent and addicted to the drug. This makes such people find it difficult to stop using such drugs.\n"
            "⦿ Delayed medical treatment: It can cause delay in the proper treatment of a disease. That is, it can make health personnel find it difficult to administer proper medical treatment to the users when the need arises and as such has to delay the health delivery process.\n"
            "⦿ Extreme mood swings and abnormal behaviour: The use of substances such as marijuana, cocaine, excessive alcohol, etc. can cause mood swings and madness or abnormal behaviour of the users.\n"
            "⦿ Loss of social respect, dignity, and personal opportunities: It can lead to loss of respect, dignity and opportunities in life. That is, it can make people have negative perceptions about the users which can cause them lose respect of people in the society. This can therefore cause them to lose opportunities such as jobs, suitors, school admission, friends, etc.\n"
            "⦿ Casual sex and sexual crimes: It can make the users become addicted and cause them engage in casual sex and rape.\n"
            "⦿ Hallucinations and false confidence: It also causes the users to get false confidence or hallucination and this can make them engage in unacceptable lifestyles such as violence, rape, armed robbery, etc. in the country. It can also lead them to commit murder in the country.\n"
            "⦿ Reproductive health complications: Abuse of substances such as alcohol, drugs, etc. can make the users suffer from impotency, miscarriage, birth of deformed babies, etc.\n"
            "⦿ Strained family and social relationships: It can lead to strained relationships with parents, friends and other people in the society. That is, parents as well as other people will reject them and regard them as bad influence on innocent people in the society.\n"
