            "(b) State three defensive skills you would use to protect yourself against substance abuse.\n"
            "(BECE 2007 Q6)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ Refusal to stick to medical advice: Attempting self-medication instead of getting a proper hospital prescription.\n"
            "⦿ Managing emotional stress: Trying to control feelings of shyness, anxiety, or anger.\n"
            "⦿ Ignorance of consequences: Not knowing the long-term harms or negative physical and mental outcomes.\n"
            "⦿ Peer pressure: Submitting to the influence or social expectations of friends who use drugs.\n"
            "⦿ Escaping economic stress: Using substances to temporarily forget systemic hardships like extreme poverty or domestic problems.\n"
            "⦿ Lack of academic self-control or curiosity: Wanting to experiment with altered states or trying to force long night study hours.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
