      PracticeQuestion(
        scenario: "Question 4: (a) Define the term decency.\n"
            "(b) Describe four behaviours considered as decent in your community.\n"
            "(c) Give three reasons for leading decent life in your community.\n"
            "(BECE 2016 Q6)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ Decency is defined as a behavioral quality, attitude, or general lifestyle that fully conforms to the recognized and acceptable ethical standards of what is right, honest, and proper within a given society.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ Respectful manual patterns: Choosing to never use the left hand when communicating, handing over objects, or greeting others.\n"
            "⦿ Academic and social integrity: Avoiding all forms of deceitful actions, such as cheating during school examination sessions.\n"
            "⦿ Communal care and kindness: Actively showing open love, kindness, hospitality, and practical assistance to fellow citizens.\n"
            "⦿ Owning up to faults: Publicly demonstrating sincere regret and taking responsibility for your wrong actions or mistakes.\n"
            "⦿ Chaste cross-gender interactions: Maintaining decent, disciplined, and morally upright interactions with peers of the opposite sex.\n"
            "⦿ Emotional self-mastery: Exercising strong emotional restraint and managing one's temper, even when under heavy provocation.\n"
            "⦿ Consistent public composure: Maintaining high personal composure, dignity, and calm behaviors in public settings.\n"
            "⦿ Modest presentation: Dressing in clean, non-revealing, and culturally respectful clothing that matches societal expectations.\n"
            "⦿ Proper table manners: Practising neat and polite eating habits when dining at home or in the presence of guests.\n"
            "⦿ Expressing gratitude: Giving immediate, heartfelt thanks and appreciation whenever a kind gesture or help is extended to you.\n"
            "⦿ Polite communication: Speaking in a polite tone and using a handkerchief or your hand to shield your mouth when coughing, yawning, or sneezing.\n\n"
            "Answer: (c)\n"
            "⦿ Gaining internal self-respect: It acts as the fundamental building block for constructing strong personal identity and self-worth.\n"
            "⦿ Earning public validation and trust: It naturally commands honor, trust, and deep respect from family elders and community leaders.\n"
            "⦿ Fostering communal tranquility: It lessens unnecessary conflict, bringing people together in harmonious and safe social environments.\n"
            "⦿ Attracting divine validation: It aligns the individual with the ethical pathways of righteousness, drawing closer to God and receiving blessings.\n"
            "⦿ Reflecting positive upbringing: It proves to the community that you have received proper home training and sound moral advice.\n"
            "⦿ Reducing societal moral crimes: It decreases the rates of moral downfalls, sexual crimes, and security threats within the direct neighborhood.\n"
            "⦿ Acting as a positive icon: It elevates you into an exemplary role model for younger children to look up to.\n"
            "⦿ Unlocking individual potential: It establishes a stellar reputation, opening clean avenues for personal networks and job opportunities.",
