            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ To preserve personal health: Staying completely away from hard drugs like cocaine, heroin, or tramadol keeps your body free from organic damage, strokes, and deadly systemic failures.\n"
            "⦿ To protect family peace: Avoiding drug habits prevents severe financial strain and emotional conflict, ensuring that your home remains a peaceful and supportive place.\n"
            "⦿ To ensure steady career progress: Refusing dangerous chemicals protects your brain functions and focus, enabling you to successfully complete your education and build a stable economic future.\n"
            "⦿ To avoid early death: Steering clear of toxic street drugs removes the critical threat of fatal overdoses, organ damage, or unexpected health failures.\n"
            "⦿ To avoid organ damage: Staying drug-free keeps vital internal structures—like your liver, kidneys, heart, and lungs—safe from toxic destruction.\n"
            "⦿ To gain deep social respect: Choosing a sober, clean life earns you a reliable reputation, ensuring that neighbors, employers, and family elders hold you in high regard.\n"
            "⦿ To build national productivity: Maintaining a healthy body and sharp mind enables you to work efficiently, helping to drive the economic growth of your community and country.",
        explanation: ".",
